==============================================================================
Vercel alias removal — uat.edforge.app
==============================================================================
Date:          2026-05-12
Operator:      shoaibrain
Sprint:        grade-level-fix T1 (closeout / infra-sunset followup)
Doc ref:       docs/infrastructure-sunset/sprint-4-vercel-env-update.md
Reason:        Remove the stale Vercel alias uat.edforge.app, which had been
               left behind by the infra-sunset/3 UAT teardown. The alias still
               pointed at a pre-sunset Vercel deployment whose bundle had the
               dead UAT us-east-2 Cognito client ID baked in. Any visitor
               (e.g. someone with a bookmark) saw the broken old SPA.

==============================================================================
Pre-state
==============================================================================
$ curl -sI -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} %{url_effective}\n" -L https://uat.edforge.app/
401 https://uat.edforge.app/
(Vercel SSO gate from a working alias serving a stale deployment.
 If you bypassed the gate, the SPA threw:
   "User pool client f9r69qrqfgpekdjfo93a8n5mu does not exist"
 because the bundle was built against the deleted UAT Cognito pool.)

$ dig +short uat.edforge.app
64.29.17.65
216.198.79.65
(Vercel edge IPs — confirming Vercel was serving the subdomain.)

==============================================================================
Action
==============================================================================
$ cd edforge-saas-frontend
$ vercel alias rm uat.edforge.app --yes
Vercel CLI 37.5.3
> Success! Alias uat.edforge.app removed [158ms]

==============================================================================
Post-state
==============================================================================
$ curl -sI -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L https://uat.edforge.app/
404
$ curl -sS https://uat.edforge.app/ | head -3
Vercel
DEPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND

(107-byte Vercel "no such alias" page. The stale UAT-Cognito-baked
 bundle is no longer reachable from anywhere on the public internet.)

==============================================================================
Remaining cleanup
==============================================================================
- External DNS record for uat.edforge.app (CNAME / A pointing at Vercel)
  is NOT removed by this action. It still resolves to Vercel's edge IPs.
  Until the operator removes it from the DNS host (Cloudflare /
  Namecheap / wherever edforge.app is managed), bookmarks still hit
  Vercel — they just get the "no such alias" page instead of a working
  app. This is a strictly better state than serving the stale broken
  bundle. Operator should delete the DNS record at next convenient
  window.

- edforge.app and www.edforge.app aliases are untouched and serving
  the current production deployment (9ztknibsq, bundle index.975eaed6.js).
  No collateral damage.

==============================================================================
